  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>It is a chemisorption <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>  is  <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math>  for adsorption. Due to electron intake in  <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>  molecule  <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">*</mi></mrow></msubsup></math>  or  <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">*</mi></mrow></msubsup></math>  (ABMO) will gain electrons and bond order of  <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>  molecule (Adsorbed) will decrease and bond length increased.<br > <br/><img src=\"assets\\st0007_380ffd146bf4.png\"/></p>"
